# playpick gave mode=battleground map=flags spec=druid:restoration style=auto
# view=844x390,touch save=carried. First healer-role spec on any battleground in
# this job's history -- all six prior battleground sessions were dps (priest:
# shadow, hunter:marksmanship, shaman:elemental, druid:feral, warlock:
# destruction, druid:balance) -- and the first genuine-touch AUTO attempt on a
# battleground: the only prior auto/battleground pull (flags/druid:feral,
# 2026-09-25) was 1280x800 desktop and silently fell back to `good` because
# isTouchMode() gates the toggle. 844x390 is real touch, so playbot's own
# play() should actually tap AUTO on rather than falling back this time.
# direction.md's [[#7]] line ("a battleground does not carry a passive body the
# way a raid does") has never seen a body that casts automatically but never
# steers -- worth knowing whether a stationary auto-healer on Ebb and Flow (the
# map where README says a carrier is the whole story) keeps its own flag
# carriers alive or gets picked off before it matters.
open
targets
shot front

tap battleground
tap map:flags
targets
shot flags-picked

tap class:druid:restoration
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot pulled
state
targets

play auto 60
shot mid1
state
bill
says

wait 5
play auto 60
shot mid2
state
bill

